> Using Date_rounding_mod

The date rounding mode is lexical: it applies to the date computations
written in the scope that declares it, not to the scopes or functions that
this scope calls from another module.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope CalleeRounds:
  output r content date

scope CalleeRounds:
  definition r equals
    (output of Date_rounding_mod.RoundDown with { -- d: |2024-01-31| }).r
  assertion r = |2024-02-29|

#[test]
declaration scope BothRound:
  output r content date

scope BothRound:
  date round up
  # The callee's rounding mode applies, not the caller's
  definition r equals
    (output of Date_rounding_mod.RoundDown with { -- d: |2024-01-31| }).r
  assertion r = |2024-02-29|

#[test]
declaration scope CallerRounds:
  output r content date

scope CallerRounds:
  date round up
  definition r equals |2024-01-31| + 1 month
  assertion r = |2024-03-01|
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope BothRound
┌─[RESULT]─ BothRound ─
│ r = |2024-02-29|
└─
```
